{
  "id": "my-calendar-batch",
  "questionId": "my-calendar-batch",
  "slug": "my-calendar-batch",
  "title": "Calendar Booking Conflicts",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Merge intervals",
  "patterns": [
    "merge intervals",
    "simulation"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "you must process bookings in the given order (this isn't a static merge problem), but you still get to choose how you store the accepted ones",
    "if you keep the accepted bookings sorted by start time, a new booking can only conflict with the accepted booking immediately before or after where it would be inserted",
    "use binary search (or an ordered structure) to find where the new booking would go among accepted bookings in O(log n), then check just its immediate neighbors for overlap",
    "remember bookings are half-open [start, end): two bookings overlap only if one's start is strictly less than the other's end on both sides"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "treating touching bookings like [10,20] and [20,30] as overlapping, forgetting the half-open [start, end) semantics",
    "checking every accepted booking on each insertion instead of only the neighbors in sorted order, which works but is needlessly slow",
    "processing bookings out of order (e.g. sorting the input first), which changes which bookings get accepted versus rejected"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're building a single calendar that starts out empty. You're given a list of proposed `bookings`, each represented as a half-open interval `[start, end)`, meaning it occupies every moment from start up to but not including end. Process the bookings one at a time, in the given order. A booking is accepted and added to the calendar if it doesn't overlap any previously accepted booking, otherwise it's rejected.\n\n**Return the total number of bookings that get rejected.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "0 <= bookings.length <= 1000",
      "bookings[i] = [start, end]",
      "0 <= start < end <= 10^9"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "empty list of bookings (answer 0)",
      "a single booking (always accepted)",
      "bookings that only touch at an endpoint (never overlap, due to half-open semantics)",
      "every booking after the first overlaps something already accepted"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
